<h1>Download Curl</h1>
<p>Curl is a drop-in replacement for the <code>curl</code> command-line tool, written in C# on .NET 10. Every file is in the rolling <code>preview</code> pre-release. The table below is <a href="https://github.com/StewartScottRogers/Curl/releases/download/preview/resources.json">resources.json</a> (version {{VERSION}}, commit {{COMMIT}}); verify a download against its SHA-256 or with <a href="https://github.com/StewartScottRogers/Curl/releases/download/preview/SHA256SUMS">SHA256SUMS</a>.</p>
<h2>Which .NET library</h2>
<p>Curl.Api is for new .NET work: an async, HttpClient-shaped client. Libcurl is for porting C or libcurl code to .NET: the libcurl API one call for one call.</p>
